Importance of Statistics in Economics
Formulation of Economic Laws - The famous
'Law of Demand' and the concept of
'Elasticity of Demand' have been developed
by the Inductive method of generalisation,
which is also based on statistical principles.
Helps in understanding and solving an economic
problem - Statistical data and statistical
methods play a vital role in understanding and
solving economic problems such as poverty,
unemployment, disparities in the distribution of
income and wealth, etc.
