Importance of Statistics in Economics
Useful to study behaviour of different economic concepts
Trend-series analysis is used to study the behaviour of
prices, production and consumption of commodities,
money in circulation, and bank deposits and clearings.
Price Analysis - Statistical surveys of prices help in studying
the theories of prices, pricing policy and price trends as
well as their relationship to the general problem of
inflation.
