Importance of Statistics in Economic Planning
At every stage of economic planning, there is a need
for figures and statistical methods.
Using statistical techniques, it is possible to assess the
amounts of various resources available in the
economy and accordingly determine whether the
specified rate of growth is sustainable or not.
Statistical analysis of data regarding an economy
may reveal certain crucial areas, like increasing rate
of inflation, which may require immediate attention.
