Importance of Statistics in Business
For Establishing a Business Unit - Before starting a
business, it is necessary to know its feasibility. It
involves detailed information about location, size of
output, availability of inputs, taxes, size of market
share, turnover, etc. Statistics provide guidelines, which
may prove to be helpful in making key decisions.
For Making Marketing Strategy - Before a product is
launched, market research team makes use of various
statistical techniques like pilot survey), to analyse data
on population, purchasing power, habits of the
consumers, competitors, pricing, etc. Such studies
reveal the possible market potential for the product.
