Statistical data should be uniform and homogeneous - It
is essential that data must be uniform and homogeneous.
Heterogeneous data are not comparable. For example,
it would be of no use to compare the heights of trees
with the heights of men because these data are of
heterogeneous nature.
Statistics is only one of the methods of studying a problem -
Statistical methods are only a means to understand any
given problem rather than a method to solve any problem.
